  "python_conversion_notes": "1. All indicators are built-in (iMA, iEnvelopes) with standard params - straightforward to replicate with ta-lib or pandas_ta. 2. The digit adjustment logic (multiply pips by 10 for 3/5 digit brokers) must be handled when converting SL/TP from pip inputs to price values. 3. Entry signals are OR-combined across 6 conditions for each direction; the buy side uses CLOSE-based MA while sell side uses OPEN-based MA - this asymmetry must be preserved. 4. One buy condition is NOT a crossover but a sustained-below check (both bar[0] and bar[1] below Envelopes 0.3 lower band). 5. Trailing stop uses a step buffer: trailing only moves if (current_price - open_price) > trailing_stop + trailing_step. 6. The EA checks total positions == 0 before entering, serving as a single-position gate. 7. The filling type fallback logic (FOK->IOC->RETURN) should map to broker-specific behavior in Python backtest. 8. Time filter is optional (InpUseHours flag).",
